  "decision_reasons": [
    "The official Terms of Service permit private storage of API responses and use in internal models, including training, evaluation and backtesting, but prohibit raw-feed resale and raw-field republication.",
    "The current OpenAPI, soccer-hub FAQ, Serie A FAQ and 2026-11-11 changelog describe GET /v1/matches/{id}/statistics as Free (with expected_goals Solo+), but the dedicated Serie A capability matrix marks the same route Edge-only. Keep the endpoint entitlement unresolved; do not assume Free access.",
    "The global pricing page is internally inconsistent: its plan introduction says Free covers the current season while its Free bullet says current plus most-recent season. The soccer hub and dedicated Serie A page both say current season only. Do not assume prior-season access.",
    "The Free tier is limited to one selected sport. The changelog dates required sport selection for new keys to 2026-10-26 and says existing keys had a grace period through 2026-11-24. A football-only scope is sufficient for this project, but no account or key was created.",
    "The public licence notice names Football-Data.org for football data, but no field-by-field upstream mapping or independent sublicensing authority for corners, yellow cards and red cards was established.",
    "The current Serie A page shows a 2026-27 standings snapshot as of 2026-11-19, but current-season per-fixture and per-field completeness for the required statistics remains unknown.",
    "The provider says completed match/player rows can be corrected after full time and advises retaining the latest source date; per-match first-observation and per-field correction timestamp semantics remain undocumented.",
    "Local receipt UTC and SHA-256 prove project possession of exact bytes before a later quote, not the provider's upstream first observation or correction history.",
    "Retention after account closure is not explicitly defined, private raw storage is not yet available in the public repository, and separate owner authorization has not been provided.",
    "The canonical rights manifest remains HOLD_NO_INTEGRATION; integration, automated capture and frozen inference remain false.",
    "2026-11-27 live follow-up: the dedicated Serie A page's league-endpoints.json registry lists GET /v1/matches/{id}/statistics as Free and says the endpoint catalogue is generated from the same registry the gateway enforces; the same page's capability matrix still lists the route as Edge. This narrows but does not eliminate the first-party documentation conflict. No authenticated Free response or provider clarification was obtained."
  ],
